\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Progress 2026-11-11 (PST): reproduced RED. A stand-in git creates a `.keep`, removes it only on SIGTERM, and spawns a child. Run through `run_git_bounded` with a 1 s bound, it left the `.keep` behind. Fix: `gitutil.run_git(..., timeout=)` now launches through `_run_in_group`, which uses subprocess.run's keywords with its own process group and reaps SIGTERM first via `reap_process_group`. `run_git_reaped` delegates to `run_git_bounded`. 13 existing tests faked `subprocess.run` for bounded git, and each now also patches `gitutil._run_in_group` with the same fake (one line per site). Commit bb29a7b140a in worktree fix-git-kill. make verify is running.","timestamp":1794445563441596908},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"HANDOFF STATE 2026-11-11 (PST): CLOSED (class preexisting) through the completion gate. Fix merged as Gerrit 3356 at `d779ed59793`. Root cause: every bounded git call reached git through `gitutil.run_git(..., timeout=)` → `subprocess.run`, whose timeout SIGKILLs only git itself. `run_git` now runs any call that has a timeout in its own process group (`_run_in_group`, which takes subprocess.run's keywords) and reaps the group SIGTERM first. `run_git_reaped` delegates to it. Test `tests/unit/test_bounded_git_group_reap.py` fails on the pre-fix code: the `.keep` stays behind. Note for future tests: a test that fakes `subprocess.run` for a bounded git call must also patch `gitutil._run_in_group`. 15 test files were updated that way. Nothing is left open on this ticket.","timestamp":1794456978104609550}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1794427149318938547,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"99ad741a-3b03-4c30-afdc-a58305fb1c3b","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"51e0-5038-bf00-4653"},{"link_uuid":"0fa8a2f0-e450-411b-80bb-e10021487800","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"e1b5-8473-d98b-42ac"}],"description":"## Problem\n\n`gitutil.run_git_bounded` runs git through `gitutil.run_git` → `subprocess.run(..., timeout=...)`. When the bound expires, CPython SIGKILLs only the direct `git` process (`process.kill()` then `wait()`). That causes two problems:\n\n- The git process cannot run its signal cleanup. `git fetch` registers a handler that removes its `objects/pack/pack-*.keep` file on signal, and SIGKILL bypasses it.\n- Children such as `index-pack`, `pack-objects`, or the transport's `upload-pack` keep running after their parent dies, reparented to init (or to rebar-mcp when it is the container's PID 1), outside rebar's write lock.\n\nA `.keep` file excludes its pack from every later repack. Until someone deletes it by hand, that pack is never consolidated.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Production MCP tickets clone, inspected 2026-11-11: 12 `.keep` files, all reading `fetch-pack <pid> on <container-host>`, dated 2026-09-05 through 2026-09-15 UTC, no fetch running. Removed during the maintenance repair for bug `nickelic-lazuline-gonolek`.\n- Local reproduction: a stand-in `git` that held a lock and had a child process, run through a `subprocess.run` timeout, left the lock behind and its child reparented to PID 1. The same stand-in under SIGTERM-first process-group reaping (`rebar._proc.reap_process_group`) cleaned up both.\n\n## Root cause\n\nOnly the explicit maintenance step (`gitutil.run_git_reaped`, added by `nickelic-lazuline-gonolek`) launches git as its own process group and reaps the group. Every other bounded git call reaches `subprocess.run`'s parent-only kill through one seam: `gitutil.run_git(..., timeout=...)`. Callers: `run_git_bounded` (sync/push fetch+merge+push, store commits via `event_commit_git._run_git`, `run_git_write`, snapshot `git_fetch`, fsck health, completion candidate, link revert, store usability) and the direct `run_git(..., timeout=...)` sites (`freshness`, `fsck_repair`, `link_revert`, reconciler `git_adapter`, code-review `assemble`).\n\n## Plan\n\nFix it at that one seam, so every bounded git call is covered without touching callers:\n\n1. `src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py`: when `run_git` gets a `timeout`, launch git with `start_new_session=True` (POSIX) via `subprocess.Popen` and `communicate(input, timeout)`; on `TimeoutExpired` or any interruption call `reap_process_group` (SIGTERM, 5 s grace, then SIGKILL) and re-raise, so `run_git_bounded`'s existing fold to code `124` and every caller's `TimeoutExpired` handling are unchanged. `check`, `capture_output`, `text`, `env`, and `input_data` keep `subprocess.run` semantics. `timeout=None` keeps the plain `subprocess.run` path.\n2. `run_git_reaped` (the maintenance step) delegates to `run_git_bounded`, so there is one group-reaping launcher instead of two.\n3. Tests that spied on `subprocess.run` for timeout-bounded git calls are retargeted to the new seam (assert the bound is still passed).\n4. `docs/concurrency.md` scale-up paragraph and ADR 0051 amendment: one sentence each stating every bounded git child is group-reaped.\n\nNo config key, env var, flag, or new lock. `runner=` seams in `push`/`sync` are unchanged (they pass `run_git`, which now reaps).\n\n## File impact\n\n- `src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py`\n- `tests/unit/test_bounded_git_group_reap.py` (new)\n- `tests/unit/test_store_write_git_timeout_c2ba.py` (spy retarget)\n- `docs/concurrency.md`, `docs/adr/0051-foreground-git-maintenance-tickets-worktree.md`\n\n## Resolution\n\nLanded as Gerrit 3356, merged `d779ed59793`. The seam is `gitutil._run_in_group`, which takes subprocess.run's keywords. 15 test files that faked `subprocess.run` for bounded git now also patch that seam with the same fake. `test_bounded_git_group_reap.py` fails on the pre-fix code: the `.keep` is left behind.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] When a bounded git child times out, its whole process group is reaped, SIGTERM first, so no git descendant outlives the call.\n- [x] A test proves that a bounded fetch interrupted by its bound leaves no `.keep` file and no surviving child process.\n- [x] [non-codebase] `make verify` passes on the change.\n  provenance: environment=local macOS worktree at the stacked change tip, rebar 0.15.1 venv, git 2.56; principal=Rebar Bot Nava, session rebar-session-3d705fec; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — make verify exited 0 (default tier 21084 passed, integration tier 218 passed) and CI cast Verified +1 on the Gerrit change","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["relates_to","e1b5-8473-d98b-42ac"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"819857f8-04bc-462e-a09c-96309f642666","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"4eed-2e15-d018-4bd6","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Bounded git timeout SIGKILLs only the parent, stranding fetch-pack .keep files and orphaning git children","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["0ce94485-6597-494a-9d04-fbd3daf05df3","07bf9142-5c70-46a3-8212-0047f6639636","6def11c4-8e4e-4ee6-938c-a1a03d19659d","9b87e9c9-f792-4ecc-8905-678e8d1937f0","48880fdc-d397-4bca-b205-31a0cdb43b9a","0fa8a2f0-e450-411b-80bb-e10021487800","c881a750-8e28-4726-abdf-b273b9127a0c","4627660e-6b6a-41a9-92ef-ca84ef316005","819857f8-04bc-462e-a09c-96309f642666","5bb3313b-47a6-489b-b4f2-5b117e49522e","1dfa4673-4913-43e6-87df-14f00c920116"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794456978104609551,"uuid":"2b74c782-bd9b-4a36-aa63-074d7af6